From: PROJ-MK-ULTRA <loudmumble@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] multikernel: raise MK_CTRL_PGTABLE_PAGES to 256

The pool identity page table allocates one page-table page per GB of pool
at 2MB pages, from a fixed array bounded by MK_CTRL_PGTABLE_PAGES (default
64). Pools larger than ~64GB exceed the array: the baseline claims the
chunk, then mk_arch_pool_chunk_added -> mk_ident_map_range fails and the
kernel returns the memory (dmesg: "Multikernel pool: removed" follows the
contig war). 256 covers ~250GB of pool.
---
 arch/x86/include/asm/multikernel.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/x86/include/asm/multikernel.h
+++ b/arch/x86/include/asm/multikernel.h
@@ -173,7 +173,7 @@
-#define MK_CTRL_PGTABLE_PAGES	64
+#define MK_CTRL_PGTABLE_PAGES	256
